                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">
                            <locus from="2r" to="22r"/>
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1171Awdana">ʿAwda nagaśt</title>
                            <note>Indicated with the title ‘Maṣḥafa bāḥr’. The text is a copy of <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/Cheren35">Karan, Karan Catholic Mission, Missione Cattolica di Cheren Ms. 35</ref>. It was used
                                for the edition in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/IHD4VC4U"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:ContiRossini1941AwdaNagast"/><title level="a">Lo ʿawda nagast scritto divinatorio etiopico</title><title level="j">Rassegna di Studi Etiopici</title><author><forename>Carlo</forename><surname>Conti Rossini</surname></author><date>1941</date><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="issue">2</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">127-145</biblScope><note type="url">http://www.jstor.org/stable/41460166</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Divination</note><note type="tag">bm:ContiRossini1941AwdaNagast</note></note><note type="tag">Divination</note><note type="tag">bm:ContiRossini1941AwdaNagast</note></bibl> with the siglum ‘CR’.</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                            <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.1">
                                <locus from="2r" to="9v"/>
                                <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1171Awdana#tables">ʿAwda nagaśt: Sixteen circular tables, each subdivided into
        sixteen parts with questions on various topics</title>
                            </msItem>
                            <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.2">
                                <locus from="10r" to="22r"/>
                                <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1171Awdana#seas">ʿAwda nagaśt: Sixteen "seas" (ባሕር፡), each containing 16
        sentences as a response to the previous questions</title>
                            </msItem>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i2">
                            <locus target="#22v"/>
                            <title>Historical note on two impostor envoys at court</title>
                            <note>The text is a copy of two fragments from an unknown manuscript containing a story of two impostor monks who 
                                presented themselves to the king (probably <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS1854Amdase">ʿAmda Ṣǝyon I</persName>) with a forged letter—purportedly 
                                from the patriarch—calling for the deposition of the metropolitan, who is named Ṗeṭros (otherwise unknown) and 
                                the appointment of one of the monks as patriarch (!) and the other as his successor. They were unmasked by 
                                ʾabbā Qozmos (possibly <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8041Qozmos">Qozmos</persName>) for whom an otherwise unknown gadl is mentioned: 
                                <foreign xml:lang="gez">በከመ፡ ይነግር፡ መጽሐፈ፡ ገድሉ፡ ለአባ፡ ቆዝሞስ፡</foreign>. Furthermore, it is narrated, that a new 
                                metropolitan with the name Philotheos (Filātewos), was appointed in the fourth year of the reign of 
                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8595SayfaAr">Sayfa ʾArʿad</persName>. Stefan Strelcyn suggests in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/N6HPGQK3"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/><title level="m">Catalogue des manuscrits éthiopiens de l’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei: Fonds Conti Rossini et Fonds Caetani 209, 375, 376, 377, 378</title><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><author><forename>Stefan</forename><surname>Strelcyn</surname></author><pubPlace>Roma</pubPlace><publisher>Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei</publisher><date>1976</date><series><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note></note><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note><citedRange unit="page">209</citedRange></bibl> that ‘Qozmos’ and ‘Filātewos’ could be identified with nos. XLI ‘Qozmos II’
                                and XLII ‘Filatewos’, as noted in ‘Liste II’ in <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/E7NY7DMZ"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Chaine1925Chronologie"/><title level="m">La chronologie des temps chrétiens de l'Égypte et de l'Éthiopie</title><author><forename>Marius</forename><surname>Chaîne</surname></author><pubPlace>Paris</pubPlace><publisher>Libraire orientaliste Paul Geuthner</publisher><date>1925</date><note type="url">https://archive.org/details/lachronologiedes0000chan/page/n5/mode/2up</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Frühgeschichte</note><note type="tag">Kalender</note><note type="tag">bm:Chaine1925Chronologie</note><note type="tag">Ägypten</note><note type="tag">Äthiopien</note></note><note type="tag">Frühgeschichte</note><note type="tag">Kalender</note><note type="tag">bm:Chaine1925Chronologie</note><note type="tag">Ägypten</note><note type="tag">Äthiopien</note><citedRange unit="page">266</citedRange></bibl>. Two notes by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3182ContiRo">Carlo Conti Rossini</persName> 
                                indicate the position of the text in the original manuscript on folia 92v and 93v (cf. <ref target="#e3"/>).</note>
                        </msItem>
